From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Three more live switches: flush draws, upload runs, async draw waits

With EDEN_UP_LIVE_SWITCHES=1 these can change while the game runs (common/live_switch.h), so one
start compares their values at a standing spot. Without it each is what env.txt gave at its first
use, for ever, with its own parsing rules, as before.

- EDEN_NX2_FLUSH_DRAWS (a number): the rasterizer submits its command buffer every N draws.
  Read at each flush check; the draw counter counts and resets for every value, so each check
  stands alone. ParseFlushDraws is the old static read character for character: digits only,
  not zero, clamped to 32..1048576, anything else the default 128. In a live plan leave the line
  out of env.txt (any value there, 128 too, picks another prepared-shader store: the name is in
  TranslationSwitches, which is left alone) and write 128 for "off" in the schedule, never 0.
  On the PS5 the check runs every 64 draws, so use multiples of 64.
- EDEN_UP_UPLOAD_RUNS (exact 1): in-order stream uploads recorded as one command, dispatch
  barriers fused (0536). A run that is open when the value goes to 0 is closed by the next thing
  recorded, as always; what a recorded command needs later (the barrier after a copy, the choice
  in a dispatch) is captured by value when it is recorded, so the worker never reads the switch.
- EDEN_UP_ASYNC_DRAW_WAITS (exact 1): a Switch 2 draw without a depth buffer waits for its
  pipeline instead of being skipped (0540). Read per draw. It only does something with
  EDEN_UP_ASYNC_TRANSLATION=1 at boot; the app warns when a schedule turns it on without that.

Drafted with an AI tool, reviewed twice (anchors of prepare-vulkan-port.py counted per file:
unchanged; parser compared on edge cases and every 7th number up to two million; stacked and
compiled with stubs). The copy guard, the heap holders and the shadow rows stay boot-fixed.

diff --git a/src/common/live_switch.h b/src/common/live_switch.h
--- a/src/common/live_switch.h
+++ b/src/common/live_switch.h
@@ -117,6 +117,15 @@
     /// present chooses on its own whether it also waits for its own frame when the GPU is
     /// behind, as it already does from the GPU's state (core/hle/service/nx2_gsv.h).
     AheadAlways,
+    /// EDEN_NX2_FLUSH_DRAWS. Each flush check uses the current draw count;
+    /// counting and reset run for every interval, including the default.
+    Nx2FlushDraws,
+    /// EDEN_UP_UPLOAD_RUNS. Pending runs drain regardless of the live value;
+    /// each recorded dispatch carries its barrier choice by value.
+    UploadRuns,
+    /// EDEN_UP_ASYNC_DRAW_WAITS. Per-draw skip/wait policy; existing jobs
+    /// are adopted, claimed back or waited for through the normal paths.
+    AsyncDrawWaits,
     Count,
 };
 
@@ -160,6 +169,21 @@
     return text != nullptr && (text[0] == '1' || text[0] == '2') && text[1] == '\0'
                ? text[0] - '0'
                : 0;
+}
+
+/// EDEN_NX2_FLUSH_DRAWS: decimal digits only, nonzero, clamped to 32..1048576.
+/// Unset, zero, a sign, whitespace or trailing text means the default 128.
+[[nodiscard]] inline s64 ParseFlushDraws(const char* value) noexcept {
+    constexpr u32 fallback = 128;
+    if (value == nullptr || value[0] < '0' || value[0] > '9') {
+        return fallback;
+    }
+    char* end = nullptr;
+    const unsigned long parsed = std::strtoul(value, &end, 10);
+    if (*end != '\0' || parsed == 0) {
+        return fallback;
+    }
+    return static_cast<u32>(std::clamp(parsed, 32UL, 1'048'576UL));
 }
 
 struct Def {
@@ -185,6 +209,9 @@
     {"EDEN_UP_COND_BACK", ParseOneOrTwo, false, -1},
     {"EDEN_UP_SWIZZLE_UNITS", ParseExactOne, false, -1},
     {"EDEN_UP_AHEAD_ALWAYS", ParseExactOne, false, -1},
+    {"EDEN_NX2_FLUSH_DRAWS", ParseFlushDraws, false, -1},
+    {"EDEN_UP_UPLOAD_RUNS", ParseExactOne, false, -1},
+    {"EDEN_UP_ASYNC_DRAW_WAITS", ParseExactOne, false, -1},
 }};
 
 /// EDEN_UP_LIVE_SWITCHES=1 (exact "1"), read once.
@@ -482,6 +509,15 @@
                             kDefs[i].name, kDefs[needs].name);
             });
         }
+        if (static_cast<Id>(i) == Id::AsyncDrawWaits && !PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_ASYNC_TRANSLATION")) {
+            // Not a live switch, so not a `needs` index: the translators are made at boot.
+            Quiet([] {
+                LOG_WARNING(Common,
+                            "Live switches: EDEN_UP_ASYNC_DRAW_WAITS needs "
+                            "EDEN_UP_ASYNC_TRANSLATION=1 at boot: its phases change nothing in "
+                            "this run");
+            });
+        }
     }
 }
 
